  "interpretation": "The floor is the MACE expected from sampling noise alone under perfect calibration; h0_upper is the one-sided 95% limit under that null. A tolerance must sit clearly above h0_upper for the endpoint to be able to detect miscalibration; otherwise report it as inconclusive rather than as a pass. Recompute at the achieved sample size before unblinding.",
